course: dictionary
lesson: 15283
title: Sincere: true and meant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sincere is an adjective, a word that describes a noun. A sincere person means what they say or feel. They are honest and true, not pretending. «Lara gave a sincere smile when she saw her friend.» Her smile was real, so she really was happy to see her friend.
explain: Sincere can also describe something you do. «Tom made a sincere apology to his sister for breaking her toy.» A sincere apology is a real one: Tom truly means sorry, and he is not just saying it to get out of trouble. To check, swap in real or honest. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: In a letter, «Yours sincerely» is a polite ending used in the UK when you know the name of the person you are writing to. It is simply how a formal letter closes. It does not mean the writer feels more than usual.
fact: Sincere means honest and true, meaning what you say or feel.
fact: «A sincere apology» means the person is really sorry, not just pretending.
fact: Sincere is an adjective, and its forms are sincere, sincerer and sincerest.
fact: «Yours sincerely» is a polite ending to a formal letter (UK).
fact: Sincere is close in meaning to honest, but it often shows that feelings are real.
exercise: «Maya gave a sincere thank you for the birthday present.» What does sincere mean here? | Pretend, just to be polite | Quick and careless | Loud and cheerful | *Real and honest
exercise: Ben says sincere means sad. Why is he wrong? | *Sincere means honest and true, not unhappy | Sincere means the same as sorry, so it is always unhappy | Sincere means very sad, like a sob | Sincere is a word for a colour
exercise: Which ending is used at the end of a formal letter when you know the name? | Sincere, love | *Yours sincerely | Sincerest hugs | Sincerely bye
test: «Lily's sincere smile showed she was truly happy to see us.» What does sincere show? | She was bored and tired | She was lost in the crowd | *Her feelings were real | She was pretending to smile
test: Which word in «She made a sincere promise to help» is the adjective that describes promise? | made | help | promise to | *sincere
exam: Which sentence uses sincere correctly, to mean real and honest? | The sincere table was made of old wood. | *The girl gave a sincere hug to her grandma. | He sincered the cake with a big knife. | We sincerely ran all the way home.
